Package: rgraphtool
Type: Package
Title: Native R/C++ Port of the Python 'graph-tool' Library
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: person("Diogo", "Melo", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "diogro@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: A standalone native R/C++ port of the Python 'graph-tool' network
    analysis library (<https://graph-tool.skewed.de/>), derived from 'graph-tool'
    release 3.9 without any Python runtime dependency. Incorporates 'graph-tool's
    C++ adjacency structure and provides multi-threaded native C++ implementations
    of Bayesian stochastic block model (SBM) inference (flat, nested, overlapping,
    weighted, layered, planted-partition, and ordered/ranked SBMs), merge-split
    MCMC posterior sampling, partition mode clustering, Bayesian model selection,
    uncertain network and triadic-closure reconstruction, network reconstruction
    from Ising, epidemic, Gaussian, and Potts dynamics, SFDP force-directed
    layouts, interactive HTML5 animations, vector/raster plotting and offline
    geographic map projections, and a public C++ extension header interface.
URL: https://github.com/diogro/rgraphtool, https://diogro.github.io/rgraphtool/
BugReports: https://github.com/diogro/rgraphtool/issues
License: LGPL (>= 3)
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports: Rcpp, grid
LinkingTo: Rcpp, BH
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), ggplot2, svglite, knitr, rmarkdown
VignetteBuilder: knitr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: C++23
